{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "USGS3DEP_loader",
    "description": "Pure-I/O data loader for USGS 3D Elevation Program (3DEP) terrain elevation at ~1/3 arc-second (~10 m) resolution. Provides static (time-invariant) terrain elevation on a geographic (longlat/WGS84, EPSG:4326) lattice, sourced from the USGS National Map ImageServer REST API as a GeoTIFF cropped to the model domain.\n\nThis is the loader half of the usgs3dep loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1/§7; bead esm-3nc.4). It is PURE I/O: it declares its source (url_template) and the file variable it reads (elevation, with units). It performs NO reprojection and NO regridding.\n\nMigration esm 0.7.0 -> 0.8.0 (this file): v0.8.0 is a clean break that REMOVED the DataLoader `grid`/`mesh` descriptor (esm-spec §8.4: 'the former native-grid descriptor was removed in v0.8.0'; esm-schema.json DataLoader is now additionalProperties:false over {kind, source, temporal, determinism, variables, reference, metadata} with no `grid` key). Accordingly the former GDD `grid` block (family/crs/dimensions/extents + the n_lon/n_lat grid parameters) has been REMOVED. Grid geometry is now ordinary data: the native geographic lattice (its lon/lat origin = the fetched bbox, its ~0.00009259° spacing, and its runtime-resolved cell counts) is documented in metadata below and is materialized downstream by `aggregate` FAQs / coupling expressions (esm-spec §8.6 — regridding is a coupling expression between two variables, not a loader/model block). The native cell counts are domain-derived: the GeoTIFF is requested at the WGS84 envelope of the model domain, so the raster width/height are resolved from the source response at load time and capped at 1000x1000 pixels per request. Reprojection (longlat identity) and conservative regridding onto a consuming grid are performed at the coupling edge via the reprojection/ and regridding/ template libraries in earthscidiscretizations, NOT here (the model half usgs3dep.esm references this file as a subsystem via {\"ref\": \"./usgs3dep_loader.esm\"}).\n\nThis is a STATIC (time-invariant) dataset: there is NO `temporal` block, so the loader seeds CONST cadence (ess-v9a.5) — the runtime fetches the GeoTIFF once per simulation domain and never refreshes it (kind: static). Cadence derives from the absence of `temporal`, orthogonal to the `kind` enum.\n\nSlope components (dzdx, dzdy) are NOT loaded here — they are derived declaratively in the regridding model usgs3dep.esm as grad(elevation, x|y).\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/usgs3dep.jl:326 (USGS3DEPFileSet, USGS3DEPSlopeFileSet, USGS3DEP constructor). Split out of the pre-migration components/earthsci_data/usgs3dep.esm (esm-tibb); grid block removed in the 0.7.0 -> 0.8.0 migration.",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "elevation",
      "terrain",
      "slope",
      "static",
      "data_loader",
      "pure-io",
      "usgs3dep",
      "dem",
      "longlat"
    ],
    "created": "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciData.jl contributors",
      "EarthSciModels migration (esm-3nc.4)"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "U.S. Geological Survey. 3D Elevation Program (3DEP). National Map Elevation Imagery Service. https://elevation.nationalmap.gov/",
        "url": "https://elevation.nationalmap.gov/"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Source: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/usgs3dep.jl:1-410 (USGS3DEPFileSet, USGS3DEPSlopeFileSet, USGS3DEP constructor). Test: test/usgs3dep_test.jl."
      }
    ]
  },
  "data_loaders": {
    "USGS3DEP_data": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "https://elevation.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/3DEPElevation/ImageServer/exportImage?bbox={bbox_west},{bbox_south},{bbox_east},{bbox_north}&size={width},{height}&format=tiff&bboxSR=4326&imageSR=4326&pixelType=F32&interpolation=+RSP_BilinearInterpolation&f=image"
      },
      "variables": {
        "elevation": {
          "file_variable": "Band1",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Terrain elevation above WGS84 ellipsoid (m). Fetched directly from the USGS 3DEP ImageServer GeoTIFF response — a single-band raster, so the GeoTIFF reader keys it 'Band1'. No-data pixels outside US territory are NaN. The slope components dzdx/dzdy are NOT loaded here: this loader is pure I/O, and the slopes are derived declaratively from this elevation field by grad equations in the regridding model (usgs3dep.esm)."
        }
      },
      "reference": {
        "citation": "U.S. Geological Survey. 3D Elevation Program (3DEP). National Map Elevation Imagery Service. https://elevation.nationalmap.gov/",
        "url": "https://elevation.nationalmap.gov/"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": ["elevation", "terrain", "slope", "static", "derived", "usgs3dep", "longlat"],
        "earthscidata_source": "src/usgs3dep.jl::USGS3DEPFileSet, src/usgs3dep.jl::USGS3DEPSlopeFileSet",
        "native_crs_epsg": "EPSG:4326 (geographic longlat / WGS84). At esm 0.8.0 the crs is documentation only — the loader no longer carries a `grid`/crs descriptor; reprojection (longlat identity) is applied at the coupling edge via reprojection/longlat.esm.",
        "native_resolution_deg": {
          "lon": 0.00009259,
          "lat": 0.00009259
        },
        "native_staggering": "Cell-centered (lon 'center', lat 'center') — 3DEP is a regular non-staggered raster. At esm 0.8.0 conservative regridding onto a consuming grid is expressed as a coupling expression (regridding/conservative_overlap.esm), not a model `regrid` block; see usgs3dep.esm and the wildlandfire.esm coupling.",
        "native_extent": {
          "lon": [-180.0, -60.0],
          "lat": [17.0, 72.0]
        },
        "resolution_arc_seconds": 0.333,
        "coverage": "US only (CONUS + Alaska + Hawaii + US territories). Cells outside US territory return NaN.",
        "url_substitutions": "bbox_{west,south,east,north} are the model-domain bounding box in decimal degrees (WGS84); {width} and {height} are pixel dimensions capped at 1000 (= min(1000, round((E-W)/resolution)) and min(1000, round((N-S)/resolution))). These substitution tokens are resolved from the simulation domain at load/fetch time (the native lon/lat cell counts are the resulting raster width/height).",
        "url_defaults": {"size_cap": 1000},
        "max_request_pixels": "1000x1000",
        "file_format": "GeoTIFF (F32 pixel type)",
        "slope_derivation": "Slope components dzdx/dzdy are derived declaratively in the regridding model usgs3dep.esm as grad(elevation, x|y) — they are NOT loaded here. This loader exposes only the single-band elevation GeoTIFF (GDAL band 'Band1').",
        "static_note": "No temporal block: kind='static' and the absence of `temporal` seed CONST cadence (ess-v9a.5). The runtime fetches the GeoTIFF once per simulation domain. Upstream DataFrequencyInfo uses two bracketing time points solely to satisfy the interp_unsafe interface; no time interpolation occurs.",
        "migration_note": "esm 0.7.0 -> 0.8.0: removed the DataLoader `grid` block (family/crs/dimensions/extents + n_lon/n_lat parameters), which the 0.8.0 schema no longer permits (clean-break removal of the native-grid descriptor, esm-spec §8.4). Native grid geometry is now documented here and materialized downstream via aggregate/coupling; no other field changed."
      }
    }
  }
}
